# 📘 Git Branching Checklist (MoneyPilot Backend)

This checklist helps track and manage all Git branches used during backend development using a professional GitFlow.

---

## 🔀 Branch Structure

* `main` → **Production-ready code only**
* `develop` → **Integration branch for all completed features**
* `feature/*` → **Each feature or task under development**
* `release/*` → (Later) Stable version preparation

---

## ✅ Feature Branch Tracking

| Branch Name                 | Purpose                               | Status |
| --------------------------- | ------------------------------------- | ------ |
| `feature/expense-entity`    | Define `Expense`, `Category` entities | ☐      |
| `feature/dbcontext`         | Set up `MoneyPilotDbContext.cs`       | ☐      |
| `feature/repository-uow`    | Implement repositories + Unit of Work | ☐      |
| `feature/expense-service`   | Add service layer for Expenses        | ☐      |
| `feature/expense-api`       | Create `ExpenseController` + CRUD     | ☐      |
| `feature/auth-setup`        | Implement JWT authentication & User   | ☐      |
| `feature/investment-module` | Investment model and service logic    | ☐      |
| `feature/budget-module`     | Budget tracking entities and API      | ☐      |

> Mark ✔ as you finish and merge each feature branch back into `develop`.

---

## 🛠 Workflow

### Start a Feature:

```bash
git checkout develop
git pull origin develop
git checkout -b feature/your-feature-name
```

### Finish a Feature:

```bash
git add .
git commit -m "Your commit message"
git checkout develop
git merge feature/your-feature-name
git push origin develop
git branch -d feature/your-feature-name
```

---

## 📦 When to Create a Release Branch

Create a `release/*` branch when you're ready to stabilize and ship a version:

```bash
git checkout develop
git checkout -b release/1.0.0
git push origin release/1.0.0
```

Then merge back into:

* `main` → final deployable code
* `develop` → so fixes aren’t lost

---

## 🧠 Pro Tips

* Keep branches small and focused.
* Use lowercase, hyphenated branch names.
* Always test before merging.
* Never push directly to `main` or `develop`.
* Use pull requests or self-merges to simulate teamwork.

---

Update this checklist regularly as you build!
